    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d486">

                <pb facs="0535" n="455" xml:id="pg455"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">832.30/214: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Brazil</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Morgan</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Rio de Janeiro</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1930-11-04T16:00:00-03:00">November 4, 1930—4
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 4:11 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>140. Mello Franco, Foreign Minister of the Provisional Government,<anchor n="22"
                        xml:id="d486-f1"/> sent his Chief of Cabinet to the Embassy today to state
                    that as the Provisional Government had not had sufficient opportunity to decide
                    whether or not they wish to renew the Naval Mission contract, they desire that
                    the Mission would continue to operate after the termination of the present
                    contract on November 6th until the Government had an opportunity to reach a
                    decision probably within 15 days.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Morgan</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
